examples.question_text:
The graph shows the water level in a tank.
(a) What was the water level at 10 am?
(b) During which interval did the level stay unchanged?
(c) Describe the changes from 9 am to 1 pm.
(d) How much did the level decrease from noon to 1 pm?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=14mm,y=2mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridgrey,xstep=14mm,ystep=10mm] (0,0) grid (4,30);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.3,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,32);
\foreach \y in {0,5,10,15,20,25,30} {\draw[black] (-0.08,\y)--(0,\y);\path (0,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\foreach \x/\lab in {0/9 am,1/10 am,2/11 am,3/12 noon,4/1 pm} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.8);\path (\x,-1) node[below,rotate=45,anchor=east,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {\lab};}
\draw[graphblue,thick] (0,10)--(1,20)--(2,20)--(3,25)--(4,15);
\foreach \p in {(0,10),(1,20),(2,20),(3,25),(4,15)} {\fill[graphblue] \p circle (1.5pt);}
\path (-0.85,15) node[rotate=90] {Water level (cm)};
\path (2,-10) node {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

